NAME
       dumpe2fs - print the superblock and block group details of an ext2/3/4 file system

SYNOPSIS
       dumpe2fs [-h] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       dumpe2fs prints what is stored in an ext4 (or ext2, ext3) file
       system's superblock: its volume name (label), UUID, state, features,
       block and inode counts, mount counts and more, followed by details of
       every block group. -h prints only the superblock part, which is
       usually all you want.

       It only reads; it changes nothing. For xfs file systems use
       xfs_info instead.

OPTIONS
       -h     Print only the superblock information.

EXAMPLES
           dumpe2fs -h /dev/vdb1 | grep -i 'volume name'

SEE ALSO
       tune2fs(8), e2label(8), e2fsck(8), xfs_info(8)
